#edb/ref 1083 #uuid "42fd1e88-b1bd-520d-91af-11e4da73aadd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121406 #edb/ref 1080 "images/40/407b19e99e4fe935cc353c18afcd8576bc4a8d6fa10f5d059ff1b4a7005f4f21.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121406 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121406 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "52848fa8-e0a8-5d95-b7e3-ee8a85dd9598" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121407 #edb/ref 1080 "images/80/800cc48a7cbe24b302e3ea0d4ddd156bd33cb1ad45d8dafbbcef20b997c24585.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121407 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121407 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6dae1c1d-e85c-5ad2-95d5-247890638d6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121408 #edb/ref 1080 "images/28/280ac039d18c0af132b0a2a85a3b94226c7ff2b310c460a1086d52402bc41865.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121408 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121408 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7839d4ad-f7d4-57b2-a944-52dd9c55849d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124194 #edb/ref 1069 "e-11021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124194 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $z = \\dfrac {\\sqrt {y+1}}{x+y}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124194 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a2c947c7-9873-5137-91ca-4fe0b42e9bb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124194 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](images/5b/5b534c95f0105645223836a1b44f38db3f14bf61425b6f53ee7815742a86a068.svg)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, y \\geq -1, \\: y \\neq -x \\big\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124195 #edb/ref 1069 "e-11022" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124195 #edb/ref 1071 "Sketch the domain of $g(x,y)=\\dfrac{1}{\\ln(x+y)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124195 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "42cbeba7-685e-5782-9695-9671d16b7f80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124195 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n![](images/68/68197b31685c209b98416f8e137dca514d7fbbf382d400688d411fa633ffd3c0.svg)\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD = \\left \\{ (x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\, : \\, y \\gt -x, \\, y \\neq 1-x \\right \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we plot the corresponding domain. \n\n- Starting with $y> -x,$ we draw a dashed line $y=-x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n\n- Then, we draw a dashed line $y=1-x$ through the shaded region.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/6a/6aa1aaeadb177cf5a80bcb12a247725cb3396586e7516c3ba30b46b03a9d2612.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124196 #edb/ref 1069 "e-11025" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124196 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124196 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59fa0287-0562-5cf2-8469-946a69dc8adf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124196 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3),$ we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,3) & =({y}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(x-7)){|}_{(10,3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(10-7) \\\\  & =9-{log}_{3}⁡(3) \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(10,3)=8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124198 #edb/ref 1069 "e-11029" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124198 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the domain of the function $z= \\dfrac{\\ln (2x+y)}{\\sqrt{x}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124198 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bdae9fe0-a491-531b-ac36-7a37d2c32f16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124198 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive,\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y>0 \\\\ x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\big\\{(x, y)\\in\\mathbb R^2 \\,:\\, 2x+y >0, \\: x > 0 \\big\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186378773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186378780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186378787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/ref 1039 "The Domain of a Function Involving Reciprocals and Radicals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124636 #edb/re