592186045417] [17592186277808 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277808 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277808 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186275623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277808 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "36c223f0-1ac5-50b8-bc16-df19662b3923" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278213 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278213 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158574" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278213 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278213 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $z=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-1$ at the point $(3,{e}^{2}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278213 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d225e24f-f8fc-5851-bdaa-9e7972c2ed2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278213 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(3,{e}^{2}),$ we substitute $x=3$ and $y={e}^{2}$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(3,{e}^{2})} & =(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-1){|}_{(3,{e}^{2})} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})-1 \\\\  & =3(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)-1 \\\\  & =3(2)-1 \\\\  & =6-1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388995 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388995 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388995 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388995 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388995 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9419d3b0-0595-5357-8a67-2ff487c67499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388995 #edb/ref 1074 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,(x,y)\\ne (0,0)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,(x.y)\\ne (0,0)\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $\\ne $ sign, the point $(0,0)$ is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we exclude the point $(x,y)=(0,0)$ and shade the plane.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/70/701c54bff1c431883f21cb980ac43f4f2f6beabb11817066a4e909d5a2663a25.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186389001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388996 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "60958810-5683-5293-9f68-2735d4937038" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388997 #edb/ref 1080 "images/65/65e29ff9fda5ad25fbbd68121d0c1a86e27a41de8890af31425208d7c38f2c2f.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388997 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388997 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "613e7132-2128-56b5-bc00-f53656e511b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388998 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c3/c30be01de07727a44fce390cfc2c56ddeed8071a7a7d64abec831a31aa2079fe.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388998 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388998 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "344a137c-9b7d-593b-8372-97e276d83d39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388999 #edb/ref 1080 "images/47/4789f1e3a4fbe0c6f23980010a0222905cb46b4ef105b02e7fba0b59fc570eeb.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388999 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759